{"schema_version":1,"seq":5,"event_id":"evt_20260525_231231_0005","run_id":"2026-05-25-generalize-stage-context-md","at":"2026-05-25T23:12:31-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"ArtifactWritten","status":"planning","payload":{"artifact_key":"plan","path":"/Users/timothy.shee/GitHub/LOCAL_worktrees/new-tech-monorepo/agent-workbench-live/worktrees/agent-workbench-live/20260525__generalize-stage-context-md/agentic-development-task-system-v3__ai/agent-workbench-live/runs/2026-05-25-generalize-stage-context-md/plan.md","summary":"template staged"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":6,"event_id":"evt_20260525_231654_0006","run_id":"2026-05-25-generalize-stage-context-md","at":"2026-05-25T23:16:54-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-001","text":"`meta` passed into `cmd_start.run` is stale after `metadata.update` on line 88 (the closure mutates the on-disk file but the local dict isn't refreshed). `_write_build_context_artifacts` must reload meta via `metadata.load(cfg, run_id)` if it needs the `base_ref_sha`.","reason":"Reading `cmd_start.py`, the `_m` closure at line 84 mutates a dict argument passed to `metadata.update`. Standard `metadata.update` patterns I've seen elsewhere in this codebase read-modify-write the file; whether they also mutate the caller's `meta` reference depends on `metadata.update`'s implementation. Safer to reload than to trust.","impact":"low. Worst case: `base_ref_sha` is missing from `build-context.md#worktree` for the first run that hits the helper. Easy to spot and fix.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":7,"event_id":"evt_20260525_231655_0007","run_id":"2026-05-25-generalize-stage-context-md","at":"2026-05-25T23:16:55-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-002","text":"Running `python -m pytest` from `agent-workbench-live/` works without a virtualenv shim or `bin/pytest` invocation. If a shim is required (analogous to `bin/pytest` patterns elsewhere in this repo family), the builder discovers it during the build stage and records the actual command in `build.md`.","reason":"The user's CLAUDE.md mentions `bin/pytest` for the `app` (Django) repo. This is a different repo (no Django). The standard pattern for `agent-workbench-live` is bare `python -m pytest`; confirming during build.","impact":"medium. Wrong invocation means the test suite isn't actually validated. Easy to catch (commands log will show the failure).","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":8,"event_id":"evt_20260525_231655_0008","run_id":"2026-05-25-generalize-stage-context-md","at":"2026-05-25T23:16:55-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-003","text":"`templates/build.md` exists at `agent-workbench-live/templates/build.md` with sensible section headings that can be inlined verbatim into `build-context.md`.","reason":"The subagent listed `templates/build.md` in its summary as a real file. The exact contents weren't quoted, but the file's existence is enough to plan against. If the contents turn out to be unsuitable (e.g. heavy boilerplate that bloats `build-context.md`), the build stage either trims at inline time or files a follow-up.","impact":"low. Worst case: `build-context.md` has a verbose inline template section; cheap to iterate.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":9,"event_id":"evt_20260525_231656_0009","run_id":"2026-05-25-generalize-stage-context-md","at":"2026-05-25T23:16:56-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-004","text":"`docs/lifecycle.md`'s `building` stage table has a structure compatible with adding a new `build-context.md` row alongside existing rows (Reads, Produces, etc.). The subagent reported a table-with-named-rows shape; this assumption holds unless the file has changed since.","reason":"Lifecycle docs are slow-changing; the subagent read the file during planning.","impact":"low. If the table shape is different, the builder adjusts in-place; the change is small.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":10,"event_id":"evt_20260525_231656_0010","run_id":"2026-05-25-generalize-stage-context-md","at":"2026-05-25T23:16:56-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-001","decision":"`build_context.build` takes `pathlib.Path` arguments and reads files internally, matching `validate_context.build`'s signature shape. Not a pure string-in function.","rationale":"Consistency with the existing curated-context builder. The brief's \"pure function takes strings\" framing was an assumption in the raw idea; `validate_context.build` is explicitly path-in, and `_read()` is the load-bearing defensive helper. Mirroring keeps cognitive overhead minimal and avoids the question \"why does this builder take strings when the other takes paths?\"","alternatives_considered":"(a) Pure string-in (raw idea's framing); (b) Mixed \u2014 paths for big artifacts, strings for `meta`.","why_not_alternatives":"(a) Introduces an inconsistency that hurts the next person reading both files. (b) is what this plan adopts for `meta` specifically \u2014 it's a dict, not a file \u2014 so the \"mixed\" critique evaporates; the substantive choice is \"paths for the markdown artifacts,\" which matches `validate_context`.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":11,"event_id":"evt_20260525_231657_0011","run_id":"2026-05-25-generalize-stage-context-md","at":"2026-05-25T23:16:57-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-002","decision":"Write `build-context.md` from `cmd_start.py`, not from a hypothetical `/build` slash command's `--init` step or from a building-stage entry hook.","rationale":"The raw idea floated both options. The brief committed to `/start`. Validating that choice during planning: there is no `/build` slash command at all (subagent investigation confirmed). The building stage is entered passively by the agent operating inside the worktree after `/start`. So `/start` is the only deterministic write point upstream of building.","alternatives_considered":"Write it on first agent-side action (e.g. lazy generation when the agent first reads the file); add a new `/build --init` slash command to symmetrize with `/shape --init` / `/plan --init` / `/validate --init`.","why_not_alternatives":"Lazy generation moves a deterministic step into the agent's responsibility \u2014 exactly what curated-context exists to prevent. Adding a new slash command is scope creep against the brief's non-goal list and adds friction for the human (one more command to remember).","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":12,"event_id":"evt_20260525_231657_0012","run_id":"2026-05-25-generalize-stage-context-md","at":"2026-05-25T23:16:57-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-003","decision":"Duplicate the helper functions `_read`, `_section`, `_HEADING_RE` (and a small variant of the DR/ASM block extractor) into `lib/build_context.py` rather than importing from `lib/validate_context.py` or extracting a shared `lib/context_helpers.py`.","rationale":"The two builders may diverge later (different sources, different filters, different output structures \u2014 followups-context.md, plan-context.md, shape-context.md will each have their own quirks). A shared base prematurely couples them. The bad-examples block in the brief explicitly flags \"edits to validate_context.py itself\" as a bad outcome; duplicating instead of refactoring honors that. The functions are 5\u201310 lines each; the duplication cost is trivial.","alternatives_considered":"Extract a shared `lib/markdown_sections.py` with `read`, `section`, `heading_re` exported; import from validate_context directly.","why_not_alternatives":"Extracting now means a third file to read and a shared API surface to maintain; the extraction is cheaper *after* the third builder lands (when the right shape is visible). Importing from validate_context creates a sibling-import cycle in a flat lib/ layout for what should be a small, self-contained file.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":13,"event_id":"evt_20260525_231658_0013","run_id":"2026-05-25-generalize-stage-context-md","at":"2026-05-25T23:16:58-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-004","decision":"Include all DR-NNN / ASM-NNN blocks from `plan.md` in `build-context.md#decisions--assumptions`, without filtering against `build.md` (which doesn't yet exist at building-entry time).","rationale":"At validate-time, `_filtered_plan_blocks` filters DR/ASM blocks against `build.md` so the reviewer sees only the decisions actually referenced. At building-entry there's no `build.md` yet, so there's nothing to filter against; the agent needs the full list to keep itself bounded. The \"filtered\" label in the brief was a copy-paste error; corrected here to \"all relevant\" in the actual heading.","alternatives_considered":"Filter against `brief.md` (which decisions does the brief mention?); leave the section empty and tell the agent to read `plan.md` if they want decisions.","why_not_alternatives":"Filtering against brief is noise \u2014 briefs typically don't mention DR-NNN IDs because the brief is code-blind. Leaving empty defeats the cache-discipline goal (agent still has to read plan.md).","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
